{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A path cut at a comment limit can expose the owner's username and local directory fragment in a public PR comment."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A local path in a link label or title can be published with the owner's username and directory layout intact."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"File URLs and paths resolved through symlinks can expose private local directory information in published reports."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A pathological run of unclosed brackets causes a measured temporary delay, with no demonstrated loss of work or outage."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An uppercase web URL containing a local path in its query can be changed to point to different content, potentially misleading its reader."}]}